### Acceptance Criteria

#### Documentation Completeness
- [ ] All identified gaps are addressed
- [ ] All required sections are documented
- [ ] Examples and use cases provided
- [ ] Cross-references added and verified

#### Technical Accuracy
- [ ] All technical details verified against codebase
- [ ] Code examples tested and validated
- [ ] API endpoints and configurations are correct
- [ ] Integration patterns match actual implementation

#### Usability
- [ ] Documentation is clear for target audience
- [ ] Examples are practical and actionable
- [ ] Navigation and structure are intuitive
- [ ] Follows documentation style guidelines

#### Quality
- [ ] Follows AsciiDoc formatting standards
- [ ] Diagrams are accurate and clear
- [ ] All links work correctly
- [ ] Grammar and spelling checked

#### Engineering Harness Compliance
- [ ] No hardcoded URLs, secrets, or environment-specific values
- [ ] Layered architecture respected (no upward imports)
- [ ] All external inputs validated at API boundary
- [ ] No sensitive data in log statements
- [ ] State types are exhaustive (sealed class/enum/discriminated union)
- [ ] Error states explicitly modeled and tested
- [ ] Configuration externalized with typed defaults
- [ ] Dependencies managed through BOM/catalog governance
- [ ] Architecture enforcement rules pass (ArchUnit/ESLint/SwiftLint/Detekt)
- [ ] Test coverage: unit + integration + error paths

